<title>UK: Rank yr pre-tx hit by exceptionals.</title>
<headline>Rank yr pre-tx hit by exceptionals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, normalised)	     24.1    vs 31.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)			12.0    vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence)		17.0    vs n/a</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-excep		    297.0    vs 408</p>
<p> Pre-tax				   65.0    vs 515.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax, pre-exceptional profits in a range between 283 and 330 million stg.</p>
<p>Rank took an exceptional charge of 232 million pounds before tax in 1996, the main elements of which were a property write-off, restructuring costs and a loss on disposals. The figures were further distorted by a change in the way the company accounts for its stake in Rank Xerox.</p>
<p>Full company name - Rank Group Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
